
# The private MyHeritage export. It carries every living person in full —
# archive's own data under site/src/data is the redacted, publishable form;
# names, birth dates, birth places — and this repository is public. The
# this is the raw source and must never be committed again.
*.log
.DS_Store
.astro/
.env
dist/
node_modules/
site/public/atlas-data.json
sources/*.ged
sources/*.gedcom

# A private build directory, so a check never reads a dist another session is
# halfway through writing. ARCHIVE_OUT=dist-verify points the gates at it.

# A PRIVATE BUILD DIRECTORY, AND EVERY NAME ONE MIGHT TAKE.
# `dist` is shared by the sessions working in this tree, so a check is pointed
# at a build of its own with ARCHIVE_OUT. `dist-verify` was that name until two
# sessions collided in it; the kit now suggests a per-session one, so the glob
# has to cover whatever it composes. Untracked build output here is also how a
# scoped `git add` picks up another session's work, which has happened in this
# estate more than once tonight.
site/dist-*/
